WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.050
Grindavík, Iceland, November 2023.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.810
Magma moves beneath the town, and
half of it drops more than a metre.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.750
Crews build earth-and-rock
barriers to turn the lava aside.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.530
August 2017, Freetown, Sierra Leone.

5
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.170
After 1,040 millimetres
of rain since July,

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.470
a slope collapses into a fast debris flow.

7
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.590
So why do some disasters leave
a community better prepared,

8
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.250
and others worse off for years?

9
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.770
Is it only the hazard's size?

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.270
In this mission, you'll draw how quality
of life falls and recovers over time

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.970
after a disaster.

12
00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.390
Then you'll follow the
stages of managing risk,

13
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:45.090
before, during and after,
through Grindavík and Freetown.

14
00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.650
Your mission: explain why one
community recovers stronger,

15
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:51.490
while another stays weaker for years.
